                    <chunk name="param_output" index="8">
                      <items count="7">
                        <item name="Access" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">1</item>
                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Tree crowns from the cloud's own vegetation returns (classes 3-5; unclassified points beside buildings when the cloud has a building class), one closed mesh per cluster of 4 m columns from 0.41 x tree height to the top, none inside a footprint. Plug into the Tree component's Geometry, one Tree per crown. Empty when the cloud has no vegetation, and not rebuilt from the cache: press Re-run.</item>
                        <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">c6f35baf-30a7-41e6-bb7c-60f4be09efeb</item>
                        <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Tree Crowns</item>
                        <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Tree Crowns</item>
                        <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                        <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                      </items>
                      <chunks count="1">
                        <chunk name="Attributes">
                          <items count="2">
                            <item name="Bounds" type_name="gh_drawing_rectanglef" type_code="35">
                              <X>888</X>
                              <Y>754</Y>
                              <W>88</W>
                              <H>33</H>
                            </item>
                            <item name="Pivot" type_name="gh_drawing_pointf" type_code="31">
                              <X>932</X>
                              <Y>771.3333</Y>
                            </item>
                          </items>
                        </chunk>
                      </chunks>
                    </chunk>
                    <chunk name="param_output" index="9">
                      <items count="7">
                        <item name="Access" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">1</item>
                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">The vegetation the crowns leave out — hedges, shrubs, young trees from 0.5 m up — one closed mesh per cluster of 2 m columns that stand on the ground and rise to the tallest return, none under a crown, none inside a footprint. Plug into the Tree component's Geometry with a shrub species (Hedge / shrub). Read only from a cloud that classifies vegetation (ASPRS 3-5): where the trees are unclassified points beside buildings, a low one would also be a car or a fence, so none is read. Lawn under 0.5 m is not geometry: it is the surface layers' ground cover. Together with Tree Crowns this is all the vegetation the cloud holds; the Report says what was read.</item>
                        <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">dab237ed-24af-4a64-9b39-0839851b0db6</item>
                        <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Low Vegetation</item>
                        <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Low</item>
                        <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                        <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                      </items>
                      <chunks count="1">
                        <chunk name="Attributes">
                          <items count="2">
                            <item name="Bounds" type_name="gh_drawing_rectanglef" type_code="35">
                              <X>888</X>
                              <Y>788</Y>
                              <W>88</W>
                              <H>33</H>
                            </item>
                            <item name="Pivot" type_name="gh_drawing_pointf" type_code="31">
                              <X>932</X>
                              <Y>804.6667</Y>
                            </item>
                          </items>
                        </chunk>
                      </chunks>
                    </chunk>
                    <chunk name="param_output" index="10">
                      <items count="6">
                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">The same vegetation as individual trees, ONE mesh: a round crown on a short trunk each, standing where the canopy of the cloud's vegetation returns peaks (1 m raster, 3 m and taller, none inside a footprint, at most the 20,000 tallest). For looking at and for a render, not for a solver: Tree Crowns are the porous zones the Tree component takes. Empty when the cloud has no vegetation (the Report says why); kept with the cached surface.</item>
                        <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">c9332565-b8ef-4fe3-b15f-08f79901cf38</item>
                        <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Trees</item>
                        <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Trees</item>
                        <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                        <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                      </items>
                      <chunks count="1">
                        <chunk name="Attributes">
                          <items count="2">
                            <item name="Bounds" type_name="gh_drawing_rectanglef" type_code="35">
                              <X>888</X>
                              <Y>821</Y>
                              <W>88</W>
                              <H>33</H>
                            </item>
                            <item name="Pivot" type_name="gh_drawing_pointf" type_code="31">
                              <X>932</X>
                              <Y>838</Y>
                            </item>
                          </items>
                        </chunk>
                      </chunks>
                    </chunk>
                    <chunk name="param_output" index="11">
                      <items count="6">
                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">The WHOLE ground as one welded mesh over the whole Domain: no layer is cut out of it and no footprint is either. It is the surface's own triangulation with every triangle at the height of the ground at its corners, so where Terrain or a Layers mesh exists the two agree exactly, a flattened pond is as level here as there, and under a building it is the plane through the ground the walls stand on at the footprint's corners (not the roof). Terrain stays the ground OUTSIDE buildings and layers; this is the ground they all stand on, to look at, to drape something on or to read heights from. Not drawn in this component's preview (it lies under the other parts); kept with the cached surface.</item>
                        <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">ad452a28-8985-4fad-97b2-2954a01d9542</item>
                        <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Full Terrain</item>
                        <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Ground</item>
                        <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                        <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                      </items>
                      <chunks count="1">
                        <chunk name="Attributes">
                          <items count="2">
                            <item name="Bounds" type_name="gh_drawing_rectanglef" type_code="35">
                              <X>888</X>
                              <Y>854</Y>
                              <W>88</W>
                              <H>33</H>
                            </item>
                            <item name="Pivot" type_name="gh_drawing_pointf" type_code="31">
                              <X>932</X>
                              <Y>871.3333</Y>
                            </item>
                          </items>
                        </chunk>
                      </chunks>
                    </chunk>
                  </chunks>
                </chunk>
              </chunks>
            </chunk>
