            <chunk name="Object" index="7">
              <items count="3">
                <item name="GUID" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">7d2ddb21-f9be-45e0-8c71-fc30d4b58712</item>
                <item name="Lib" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">6c2961a3-b4b9-45a6-8474-c1c0d5dc1b86</item>
                <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Live Wind Tunnel</item>
              </items>
              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="4">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Sketch a site against the wind: a 2D lattice-Boltzmann wind tunnel that runs continuously and paints the flow into the viewport while you move buildings and probes. Nothing restarts when geometry moves.

For an urban block, cut the buildings at pedestrian height (Cut Height ≈ 1.75 m) and wire the ABL Flow the wind studies use into ABL: the tunnel then runs in that profile's speed at the cut, in its first wind direction.

A SKETCH tool: the site is a section through infinitely tall buildings (no flow over or under anything, no buoyancy), and the solver's viscosity floor runs it at a far lower Reynolds number than real air. Compare variants of a site layout with it, with Mean on (a single frame of a wake is gusty); take numbers you report from an OpenFOAM or LBM Case run.

Version 1.20.0.827

Version 1.20.0.827</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">e182b984-635d-4386-b45d-e73ce0b78828</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Live Wind Tunnel</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Live Wind Tunnel</item>
                  </items>
                  <chunks count="23">
                    <chunk name="Attributes">
                      <items count="2">
                        <item name="Bounds" type_name="gh_drawing_rectanglef" type_code="35">
                          <X>1441</X>
